1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,510
Aim: pick Barnard's Star, or type any coordinates.

2
00:00:03,710 --> 00:00:08,691
Watch: real SPHEREx images from every date become a video, filtered by detector.

3
00:00:08,891 --> 00:00:13,430
Discover: subtract two dates, and whatever moved shows up as bright and dark pairs.

4
00:00:13,630 --> 00:00:18,854
Then jump seventy-six years: from 1950 to SPHEREx, same patch of sky.

5
00:00:19,054 --> 00:00:21,665
Instant spectra, with contamination flags.

6
00:00:21,865 --> 00:00:24,153
Plus Gaia and WISE overlays on the sky map.

7
00:00:24,603 --> 00:00:28,142
Aim. Watch. Discover.
